# Driver payouts

## Single source of truth

- Read job-level rows only from `admin_driver_payout_jobs_v1`
- Read weekly rollups only from `admin_driver_payout_weekly_v1`
- Persist payout lifecycle only in `driver_payout_line_marks` (unpaid → exported → paid)
- Do not recompute client paid / driver owed in React; trust the views

## Money fields

- `client_paid_pence` = sum of succeeded `booking_payments` for the booking
- `driver_owed_pence` = COALESCE(final, estimated, payout, target) from latest `internal_leg_financials`
- Always store and transfer amounts in **pence**; format GBP only in UI/CSV export

## Wise readiness

- Secrets: `WISE_API_TOKEN`, `WISE_ENV=sandbox|production`, optional `WISE_PROFILE_ID`, optional `WISE_GBP_BALANCE_ID`
- Status: `GET /api/admin/driver-payouts/wise-status`
- Diagnose fees: `GET /api/admin/driver-payouts/wise-diagnose` (BALANCE vs BANK_TRANSFER quote options)
- Pay API: `POST /api/admin/driver-payouts/pay-wise` — recipient-first quote with `preferredPayIn=BALANCE` + `payInMethod` + balance id; batch transfers; attempt fund
- Export CSV backup: `/api/admin/driver-payouts/export-wise`
- Never send full bank numbers to the browser list UI (masked last4 only)
- Docs (personal token): API may create quotes/recipients/transfers/batches; **funding via API only for US/CA/AU/NZ/SG/MY**. UK = draft in API, fund in Wise portal.
- Quote without BALANCE pay-in defaults to BANK_TRANSFER fees (~£0.52). Manual Wise “Current account 0 / Bank 0.52” is the same pay-in menu, not a separate product path.
- Docs: https://docs.wise.com/guides/developer/auth-and-security/personal-api-token · https://docs.wise.com/guides/product/send-money/quotes/authenticated-quote · https://docs.wise.com/guides/product/send-money/use-cases/payouts-smbs

## Week boundary

- Weeks are **Europe/London** ISO weeks (`week_key` like `2026-W45`)
- Settlement timestamp = `completed_at` else `scheduled_at`
